y":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- reproducible in v4.6.stable.fedora [89cea1439]\n- reproducible in v4.6.stable.official [89cea1439]\n- worked in v4.4.1.stable.official [49a5bc7b6] but MRP was created in 4.6\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.6.stable (89cea1439) - Fedora Linux 43 (KDE Plasma Desktop Edition) on Wayland - X11 display driver, Multi-window, 1 monitor - Vulkan (Mobile) - integrated AMD Radeon 780M Graphics (RADV PHOENIX) - AMD Ryzen 7 PRO 8840U w/ Radeon 780M Graphics (16 threads) - 29.99 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\n$FileDialog.show() does not use the native mode on android (14, pixel 4 with lineage) which it did on previos godot versions.\n\nIt's closely related to #115983 as the mentioned (Method 3) workaround for android seems to work for me as well, but I am not allowed to reopen it.\n\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- add a FileDialog to root node\n- set FileMode to \"Open File\", Access to \"File System\", Use Native System and visible to true\n- start in remote deploy\n\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n\n- unsure whether OS.request_permissions() is needed when using remote deploy, did not work with it included as well\n[Archive.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/25328750/Archive.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo